shall we get the certificate of transfer(mutation) on nala conversion land in telangana?

Yes, you can obtain a Mutation Certificate (Certificate of Transfer) for NALA (Non-Agricultural Land Assessment) converted land in Telangana. 

The process depends on whether the property is registered in an urban or rural area: 

Urban/Municipal Areas (GHMC/CDMA): Since June 16, 2021, mutation is auto-initiated at the time of registration. A mutation fee (typically 0.1% of document value) is collected by the Sub-Registrar along with registration fees. Once approved by the Municipal Commissioner, the digitally signed certificate can be downloaded from the CDMA Portal or the GHMC website.

Rural Areas (Panchayats): For non-agricultural properties in rural areas, you may need to apply through Meeseva or directly to the local Gram Panchayat to update the records and receive the certificate.

Dharani Portal: If the land was recently converted from agricultural to non-agricultural through the NALA module on Dharani, the mutation for the change in land use is handled within that system. 

Key Documents Required:
Registered Sale Deed or Title Deed.
NALA Conversion Order/Receipt.
Latest Property Tax or Vacant Land Tax (VLT) receipt.
Encumbrance Certificate (EC). 
